OpenCode JSON DB Context — repository marker

OpenCode V2 recognizes opencode.jsonc, AGENTS.md, and .opencode/agents, commands and skills.
The repository ships with MCP disabled until the user completes an interactive setup:
- macOS/Linux: ./setup.sh
- Windows PowerShell: .\setup.ps1

Setup discovers or offers a compatible Python runtime, verifies/install required drivers
only with explicit approval, then writes .opencode/opencode.jsonc (Git-ignored)
for the local operating system. Re-run setup when moving the repository to another machine.

Credentials or dotenv without an explicit scope export all accessible non-system SQL databases by default.
Use .local/*.env for credential import without transmitting its content to the model.
The default workflow is read-only relational SQL inspection and a single JSON in export/.
MongoDB and other non-relational databases are not supported.
